.TH AVR\-FIREWALL\-IMPORT 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-firewall-import \- Append or replace this scope's rules from a portable JSON file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr firewall import
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Append or replace this scope's rules from a portable JSON file.
.PP
Import a console-compatible JSON policy into one organization or repository. Append skips duplicates and supplied defaults. Replace uses the file's default; without one, repository defaults inherit and organization defaults are retained. Every import is validated before applying. Use --dry-run to review changes. Replace prompts for confirmation; --yes is required with stdin or automation. If the policy changes after preview, the import fails without overwriting it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fICHOICE\fR
(choices: append, replace; default: append)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Validate and summarize changes without applying them.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fITEXT\fR
Policy file, or - to read stdin. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug; defaults to the configured organization.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository ID or owner/repo. If provided, uses repository scope.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip replacement confirmation.
